lf\u2011promoting than collegial.\n**Candidate\u202fC** \u2013 Crew cooperation:\u202fHe is regarded as egocentric, indicating limited willingness to work cooperatively with others in the cockpit.\nProfessional communication:\u202fHe has difficulty communicating ideas, which can hinder clear, respectful exchanges with fellow crew.\n**Candidate\u202fD** \u2013 Crew cooperation:\u202fHe is described as a loner and is known to have a hot temper, both of which can undermine teamwork and a positive crew environment.\nProfessional communication:\u202fHe is regarded as a know\u2011it\u2011all, a trait that often leads to dismissive or overly authoritative communication rather than collaborative dialogue.", "thoughts": "We need to answer the specific question: observations regarding crew cooperation and professional communication style for Candidates A, C, and D. Use explicit facts from notes.\n\nFrom notes:\n\n- Candidate A: regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas, regarded as being not open to new ideas, also \"very good leadership qualities\". Also \"show-off\" suggests poor crew cooperation, maybe communication style not collaborative. No explicit mention of communication style, but \"show-off\" implies possibly poor professional communication.\n\n- Candidate C: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education. Also \"keeps calm in a crisis\". So crew cooperation likely low due to egocentric and communication difficulty.\n\n- Candidate D: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper, considered a loner, moody. So crew cooperation likely poor, professional communication may be affected by hot temper and know-it-all attitude.\n\nThus answer with observations for each candidate, citing facts."}
